Chapter 3
Probability, expected loss, unexpected loss and the maximum possible
الاحتمال والخسارة المتوقعة والخسارة غير المتوقعة والحد الأقصى الممكن
Chapter 2 supplied volatility and time. This chapter turns them into the three numbers every risk assessment produces: what a risk costs on average, how much worse than average a bad year can plausibly be, and how bad the worst conceivable outcome is.
The three are not alternatives. They answer different questions, they are covered by different things — reserves, capital, and the responses of Chapter 5 — and a risk report that gives only one of them is incomplete. The arithmetic is simple; the discipline is in knowing which figure answers which question, and in knowing what the probabilities are actually worth.
Figure F803-01 is your map.
Figure F803-01. Chapter 3 roadmap: where probabilities come from, and the three losses they produce.
